md`# brain-deployer

The deployer is the one Worker that holds the Cloudflare API token: it distils module source to Worker code, deploys it, and holds a deploy until the owner approves it. It checks each deploy, puts back what fails, keeps a new kernel or core on probation until the owner confirms it, and serves a plain page that works when nothing else does.

Until 2026-10-07 the deployer was called the guard, and until 2026-10-08 its Worker was \`BASE-guard\`. The Worker is now \`BASE-deployer\`. A Brain installed before then keeps \`BASE-guard\` until it is moved (see Moving to a new Worker name). These old spellings are still read: the header \`x-brain-guard\`, the binding \`GUARD\`, the cell \`guard\`, the role and caller \`guard\`, and \`"guard"\` in a rule.

\`deployer_service\` is deployed once, by the installer. Nothing on the Brain can change it afterwards: \`deployerAllows\` and the role check in \`deployerOps\` refuse any apply that names it.`
// %%
deployer_service = cloudflare.Service("deployer", deployerFn, {
  role: "deployer",
  crons: ["* * * * *"],
  flags: ["global_fetch_strictly_public"],
  scheduled: () => deployerOps.tick()
})
// %%
md`## What an apply may touch

\`deployerAllows\` is the rule for a recipe. The kernel and the core do not pass through it: they are deployed by role, under probation.`
// %%
deployerAllows = (row) => {
  // brain-guard: the deployer's name before 2026-10-08.
  const reserved = new Set(["brain", "brain-deployer", "brain-guard", "brain-core"]);
  const kinds = new Set(["worker", "r2_bucket", "vectorize_index"]);
  if (row.op === "unchanged") return null;
  const [kind, name] = row.key.split("/");
  if (reserved.has(name)) return `resource name "${name}" is reserved`;
  if (!kinds.has(kind)) return `unknown resource kind "${kind}"`;
  if (!/^brain-x-[a-z0-9-]{1,40}$/.test(name)) return `resource name "${name}" must match brain-x-[a-z0-9-]`;
  // brain-m-… is a member's Worker, and the core binds brain-x-m-… under the same name.
  if (name.startsWith("brain-x-m-")) return `resource name "${name}" is in the members' names`;
  if (kind === "r2_bucket" && row.op === "delete" && row.objects > 0) return `bucket "${name}" holds ${row.objects} objects`;
  return null;
}
// %%
md`## Probation

One transition function for a kernel or core update, driven by the deployer's one-minute cron and by \`infra.confirm\`. Times are milliseconds.`
// %%
nextKernelState = (s, event) => {
  // 10 minutes unless the deployer's config sets probationMs, which a test Brain does.
  const PROBATION_MS = event.probationMs ?? 10 * 60 * 1000;
  const span = PROBATION_MS % 60000 ? PROBATION_MS / 1000 + " seconds" : PROBATION_MS / 60000 + " minutes";
  if (s.state !== "probation") return s;
  if (event.type === "confirm") return { state: "confirmed", version: s.version, lastGood: s.version };
  if (event.type === "tick") {
    const fails = event.healthy ? 0 : s.fails + 1;
    if (fails >= 2) return { state: "rolled-back", version: s.lastGood, lastGood: s.lastGood, reason: "health check failed twice" };
    if (event.now - s.since >= PROBATION_MS) return { state: "rolled-back", version: s.lastGood, lastGood: s.lastGood, reason: "not confirmed in " + span };
    return { ...s, fails };
  }
  return s;
}
// %%
md`## Deploying

\`deployerOps\` is everything the deployer does to Cloudflare. A Worker's name in an apply is its logical name (\`brain\`, \`brain-core\`, \`brain-x-NAME\`); the script name on Cloudflare replaces \`brain\` with this Brain's base name, so two Brains can share an account.

Each Worker gets a key when it is first deployed. The deployer presents it to reach that Worker from the internet, and the Worker presents it to the core to say which Worker it is.`
// %%
md`## Logs and Cloudflare permissions

Added 2026-10-08. The deployer turns Workers Logs on for each script and Cloudflare's own line per invocation off (\`OBSERVABILITY\`, \`ensureLogs\`). The setting belongs to the script: Cloudflare took it from the upload of a new script and ignored it in the upload of a version, so 14 of the 17 scripts of cb4 kept no logs after the first deploy of this change. \`redistil\` sets it on each script the deployer has a row for, a member's Worker and one it keeps no source of included. A deploy of a member's Worker sets it too.

A service that declares \`cloudflare: ["GROUP"]\` gets a Cloudflare API token (\`tokenFor\`, \`mint\`): held for the owner also when deploys need no approval, refused for a member and for a group that is not in \`GROUPS\`. The value is in the binding \`CF_TOKEN\` of that Worker and nowhere else. The rows \`token/WORKER\` hold the token's id, groups and end; \`audit/tokens\` holds each mint, roll and delete. A token is kept across deploys while its groups are the declared ones and it has more than 30 days left of its 90. A version that is put back gets a new token when the one it was deployed with was deleted (\`remint\`). The row of what is live is written first, with no token; when the mint or the bind fails, the line is \`token.mint-failed\` and each tick of the deployer tries again.

The deployer's own token needs the permission \`Account API Tokens Write\` to mint, and each group it hands out.

The deployer writes a line for each step of a deploy with the \`log\` cell: \`deploy.uploaded\`, \`deploy.deployed\`, \`deploy.probation\`, \`deploy.confirmed\`, \`deploy.unhealthy\` with what the last health check answered, \`deploy.put-back\` with the reason, \`deploy.refused\`, \`deploy.waiting\`, \`deploy.removed\`, \`deploy.failing\`, \`deploy.logs-on\`, \`token.mint\`, \`token.roll\`, \`token.delete\`, \`token.mint-failed\`. A member's deploy writes \`deploy.deployed\` and \`deploy.put-back\`. The \`reason\` of a put-back can be Cloudflare's own text about the code that was sent; it is not text a caller of a method sent.`
// %%
deployerOps = {
  const text = (v) => JSON.stringify(v);
  const jsonType = { "content-type": "application/json" };
  const sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));
  // The deployer's own script: BASE-deployer, or BASE-guard on a Brain installed before 2026-10-08. The installer says which.
  const selfScript = () => config.self || config.base + "-guard";
  const actual = (logical) => (logical === "brain-deployer" ? selfScript() : config.base + logical.slice("brain".length));
  const script = (logical) => "/workers/scripts/" + actual(logical);
  const urlOf = (logical) => `https://${actual(logical)}.${config.subdomain}.workers.dev`;
  const randomKey = () => [...crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(32))].map((b) => b.toString(16).padStart(2, "0")).join("");
  const api = async (method, path, body, headers = {}) => {
    const r = await fetch("https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/" + config.account + path, {
      method,
      headers: { authorization: "Bearer " + (await secrets.CF_API_TOKEN), ...headers },
      body
    });
    const j = await r.json().catch(() => ({}));
    if (!r.ok || j.success === false) throw new Error(`${method} ${path} ${r.status} ${text(j.errors || []).slice(0, 300)}`);
    return j.result;
  };
  const call = (logical, key, path, init = {}, version) => {
    // x-brain-guard: the name a Worker deployed before 2026-10-08 reads.
    const headers = { "x-brain-deployer": key, "x-brain-guard": key, ...(init.headers || {}) };
    if (version) headers["Cloudflare-Workers-Version-Overrides"] = `${actual(logical)}="${version}"`;
    return fetch(urlOf(logical) + path, { ...init, headers, redirect: "manual" });
  };
  // What the last health check of a Worker on the internet answered, for the log line of a deploy that is put back.
  let lastHealth = "";
  const healthy = async (logical, key, hash, version) => {
    try {
      // A member's Worker has no address on the internet: the core asks it over its binding.
      if (logical.startsWith("brain-m-")) {
        const j = await toCore("service.health", { worker: logical });
        return !!j && j.ok === true && (!hash || j.hash === hash);
      }
      const r = await call(logical, key, "/xrpc/_health", {}, version);
      if (!r.ok) return (lastHealth = "status " + r.status), false;
      const j = await r.json();
      lastHealth = "hash " + String(j.hash).slice(0, 12);
      return j.ok === true && (!hash || j.hash === hash);
    } catch (e) {
      lastHealth = "threw " + String((e && e.message) || e).slice(0, 120);
      return false;
    }
  };
  const waitHealthy = async (logical, key, hash, version) => {
    // 60 s. At 30 s two deploys of one Worker were put back while Cloudflare still answered with the version
    // before (2026-10-06 09:30 and 09:33); the third took 25 s.
    for (let i = 0; i < (config.pollTries || 40); i++) {
      if (await healthy(logical, key, hash, version)) return true;
      await sleep(config.pollMs ?? 1500);
    }
    log({ at: "deploy.unhealthy", target: logical, hash, version: version || "live", last: lastHealth });
    return false;
  };
  const toCore = async (nsid, input) => {
    const core = await rows.get("worker/brain-core");
    if (!core || !core.hash) return null;
    const r = await call("brain-core", core.key, "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain." + nsid, { method: "POST", headers: jsonType, body: text(input) });
    return r.ok ? r.json() : null;
  };
  const note = (key, body) => toCore("inbox.append", { source: "deployer", key, body }).catch(() => null);
  // This deployer's own hash, set by deployerFn on each request. It names the distiller: a Worker's code is a function of
  // its source and of the deployer that distilled it.
  const self = { hash: null };
  // The source kept for each module is the source of what is running. A version put back takes its source with it.
  const keptSources = async () => (await rows.list("source/")).filter((r) => !r.value.stale).map((r) => ({ module: r.key.slice("source/".length), ...r.value }));
  const sourcePutBack = async (logical, hash) => {
    for (const { key, value } of await rows.list("source/")) {
      if (value.worker !== logical || (value.hash === hash && !value.stale)) continue;
      if (value.prev && value.prev.hash === hash) await rows.put(key, { ...value.prev, worker: logical, prev: null });
      else await rows.put(key, { ...value, stale: true });
    }
  };
  const shell = async (request) => {
    const core = await rows.get("worker/brain-core");
    if (!core || !core.hash) return new Response(text({ error: "NotReady", message: "the core is not deployed" }), { status: 503, headers: jsonType });
    const query = new URLSearchParams({ path: "shell/index.html", public: "true", type: "text/html; charset=utf-8" });
    const r = await call("brain-core", core.key, "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.static.put?" + query, { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "text/html; charset=utf-8" }, body: request.body, duplex: "half" });
    return new Response(r.body, { status: r.status, headers: { "content-type": r.headers.get("content-type") || "application/json", "access-control-allow-origin": "*" } });
  };
  const currentVersion = async (logical) => {
    const d = (await api("GET", script(logical) + "/deployments")).deployments[0];
    return (d.versions.find((v) => v.percentage === 100) || d.versions[0]).version_id;
  };
  const setVersions = (logical, versions) =>
    api("POST", script(logical) + "/deployments", text({ strategy: "percentage", versions }), jsonType);
  const settings = async () => (await rows.get("settings")) || { approval: true };
  // Workers Logs are on for every Worker, and Cloudflare's own line per invocation is off. That line stores the
  // request's headers and its whole URL: x-brain-deployer and x-brain-guard (a Worker's key), x-brain-origin, and the
  // code in /link?code=… were stored in clear (tried 2026-10-08, logging-research.md). What a Worker writes with
  // console.log is kept, and the core writes one line a call from a list of names.
  // With the invocation line off Cloudflare still stores, beside each line a Worker writes, the method and URL of
  // the call with its query string; not headers, not the body. It redacts some values by name or shape, by a rule it
  // does not document. So: no long-lived secret in a path or a query string. A short-lived single-use code may be.
  // Keep the line off: x-brain-deployer, x-brain-guard, x-brain-origin and x-brain-session would be stored in clear.
  const OBSERVABILITY = { enabled: true, logs: { enabled: true, invocation_logs: false } };
  // The setting is the script's, not a version's: Cloudflare takes it from the upload of a new script and ignores it
  // in the upload of a version (seen 2026-10-08). For a script that exists it is set here, when it is not already.
  const logsOn = (o) => !!o && o.enabled === true && !!o.logs && o.logs.enabled === true && o.logs.invocation_logs === false;
  const ensureLogs = async (logical) => {
    if (logsOn((await api("GET", script(logical) + "/script-settings")).observability)) return false;
    await api("PATCH", script(logical) + "/script-settings", text({ observability: OBSERVABILITY }), jsonType);
    log({ at: "deploy.logs-on", target: logical });
    return true;
  };

  // Cloudflare permissions. A service declares the permission groups it needs (cloudflare: ["…"]). The deployer mints
  // an account token of exactly those groups, for this account, that ends in 90 days, and binds its value to that
  // Worker alone as CF_TOKEN. The value is not kept anywhere else and no method returns it. The deployer keeps the
  // token's id, its groups and when it ends (token/WORKER), and writes each mint, roll and delete to audit/tokens.
  // A service may declare only the groups in GROUPS.
  const GROUPS = ["Workers Observability Read", "Workers Tail Read"];
  const DAY = 86400000, TOKEN_DAYS = 90, ROLL_DAYS = 30;
  const audit = async (event, logical, t) => {
    const row = { at: Date.now(), event, worker: logical, token: t.id, groups: t.groups, expires: t.expires };
    log({ at: "token." + event, target: logical, token: t.id, groups: t.groups.join(", ") });
    await rows.append("audit/tokens", row, 500);
    await note(`token/${logical}/${t.id}/${event}`, row);
  };
  const mint = async (logical, groups) => {
    const all = await api("GET", "/tokens/permission_groups");
    const ids = groups.map((g) => {
      const found = all.find((p) => p.name === g && (p.scopes || []).includes("com.cloudflare.api.account"));
      if (!found) throw new Error(`Cloudflare has no account permission group "${g}"`);
      return { id: found.id };
    });
    const expires = Date.now() + TOKEN_DAYS * DAY;
    const t = await api("POST", "/tokens", text({ name: `${actual(logical)}: minted by ${selfScript()}`, policies: [{ effect: "allow", resources: { ["com.cloudflare.api.account." + config.account]: "*" }, permission_groups: ids }], expires_on: new Date(expires).toISOString().slice(0, 19) + "Z" }), jsonType);
    return { id: t.id, value: t.value, groups, expires };
  };
  // To end a token it is deleted. A rolled value was seen to answer after the roll (2026-10-08).
  const dropToken = async (logical, t) => {
    await api("DELETE", "/tokens/" + t.id).catch(() => null);
    await audit("delete", logical, t);
  };
  // The token for a deploy: the one held, while its groups are the declared ones, Cloudflare still has it and it has
  // more than 30 days left; else a new one. `binding` goes in the upload. done() after the version is live: the row,
  // and the token before is deleted. undo() when the deploy is put back.
  const tokenFor = async (logical, want, existing) => {
    const had = await rows.get("token/" + logical);
    if (!want.length) return { binding: [], id: null, done: async () => { if (had) (await dropToken(logical, had), await rows.delete("token/" + logical)); }, undo: async () => {} };
    const keep = had && existing.has("CF_TOKEN") && text(had.groups) === text(want) && had.expires - Date.now() > ROLL_DAYS * DAY && (await api("GET", "/tokens/" + had.id).then((t) => t.status === "active", () => false));
    if (keep) return { binding: [{ type: "inherit", name: "CF_TOKEN" }], id: had.id, done: async () => {}, undo: async () => {} };
    const t = await mint(logical, want), held = { id: t.id, groups: t.groups, expires: t.expires };
    let kept = false;
    return {
      binding: [{ type: "secret_text", name: "CF_TOKEN", text: t.value }],
      id: t.id,
      done: async () => {
        kept = true;
        await rows.put("token/" + logical, held);
        await audit(had && text(had.groups) === text(want) ? "roll" : "mint", logical, held);
        if (had) await dropToken(logical, had);
      },
      undo: async () => void (kept || (await api("DELETE", "/tokens/" + t.id).catch(() => null)))
    };
  };

  const uploadAsset = async (logical, html) => {
    const bytes = new TextEncoder().encode(html);
    const hash = (await sha256(html)).slice(0, 32);
    const session = await api("POST", script(logical) + "/assets-upload-session", text({ manifest: { "/index.html": { hash, size: bytes.length } } }), jsonType);
    if (!session.buckets || !session.buckets.length) return { jwt: session.jwt, hash };
    let binary = "";
    for (let i = 0; i < bytes.length; i += 0x8000) binary += String.fromCharCode.apply(null, bytes.subarray(i, i + 0x8000));
    const form = new FormData();
    form.append(hash, new File([btoa(binary)], hash, { type: "text/html" }));
    const r = await fetch(`https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/${config.account}/workers/assets/upload?base64=true`, {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { authorization: "Bearer " + session.jwt },
      body: form
    });
    const j = await r.json().catch(() => ({}));
    if (!j.success || !j.result || !j.result.jwt) throw new Error("asset upload " + r.status + " " + text(j.errors || []).slice(0, 200));
    return { jwt: j.result.jwt, hash };
  };

  const sqlDatabase = async () => {
    const known = await rows.get("sql");
    if (known) return known;
    const name = actual("brain-sql");
    const found = ((await api("GET", "/d1/database?name=" + encodeURIComponent(name))) || []).find((d) => d.name === name);
    const id = found ? found.uuid : (await api("POST", "/d1/database", text({ name }), jsonType)).uuid;
    await rows.put("sql", id);
    return id;
  };

  // The table database: a D1 database named as brain-db's script is, bound to brain-db alone.
  const ownDatabase = async (logical) => {
    const known = await rows.get("db/" + logical);
    if (known) return known;
    const name = actual(logical);
    const found = ((await api("GET", "/d1/database?name=" + encodeURIComponent(name))) || []).find((d) => d.name === name);
    const id = found ? found.uuid : (await api("POST", "/d1/database", text({ name }), jsonType)).uuid;
    await rows.put("db/" + logical, id);
    return id;
  };

  // Bindings are built here from the resources a service declares. Nothing the tab sends is bound as given.
  const bindingsFor = async (w, key, existing, given, token = []) => {
    const m = w.meta, tier = m.role === "kernel" || m.role === "core";
    const out = [];
    // Only the kernel's and the core's own keys are bound, from the installer or made here. A secret the owner set
    // is never bound: a Worker asks secret.get for it while it runs, and the secret's rule decides.
    // The signing key has two names (SESSION_KEY; before 2026-10-07 COOKIE_KEY) and one value, and the kernel reads
    // either. Cloudflare does not give a bound value back, so a name that is not held cannot be copied from the other:
    // it is left unbound. A random value under SESSION_KEY would sign each person out. With neither held, one new
    // value is bound under both.
    const twin = { SESSION_KEY: "COOKIE_KEY", COOKIE_KEY: "SESSION_KEY" };
    const held = (name) => typeof given[name] === "string" || existing.has(name);
    let signing = null;
    for (const name of tier ? m.secrets : []) {
      if (typeof given[name] === "string") out.push({ type: "secret_text", name, text: given[name] });
      else if (existing.has(name)) out.push({ type: "inherit", name });
      else if (twin[name] && m.secrets.includes(twin[name]) && held(twin[name])) continue;
      else out.push({ type: "secret_text", name, text: twin[name] ? (signing ??= randomKey()) : randomKey() });
    }
    const uses = (r) => m.resources.includes(r);
    // Every Worker's rows are in one D1 database of the Brain, made on first use. Only the deployer has a Durable Object.
    if (uses("rows")) out.push(existing.has("SQL") ? { type: "inherit", name: "SQL" } : { type: "d1", name: "SQL", id: await sqlDatabase() });
    if (uses("database")) out.push(existing.has("DB") ? { type: "inherit", name: "DB" } : { type: "d1", name: "DB", id: await ownDatabase(m.worker) });
    if (uses("blobs")) {
      const bucket = actual("brain-blobs");
      if (!existing.has("BLOBS")) await api("POST", "/r2/buckets", text({ name: bucket }), jsonType).catch((e) => { if (!/exist|10004/i.test(e.message)) throw e; });
      out.push({ type: "r2_bucket", name: "BLOBS", bucket_name: bucket });
    }
    if (uses("inbox") || uses("xrpc") || uses("sql") || uses("core") || (m.secrets.length && !tier)) out.push({ type: "service", name: "CORE", service: actual("brain-core") });
    // "guard": the cell's name in a source distilled before 2026-10-08.
    if (uses("deployer") || uses("guard")) out.push({ type: "service", name: "DEPLOYER", service: actual("brain-deployer") });
    if (uses("assets")) out.push({ type: "assets", name: "ASSETS" });
    // Browser Run. The name is the one the wrapper's workers cell reads for "cf-browser-run" (see emit in cloudflare-iac).
    if (uses("browser")) out.push({ type: "browser", name: "X_CF_BROWSER_RUN" });
    for (const name of existing) if (name.startsWith("X_") && name !== "X_CF_BROWSER_RUN") out.push({ type: "inherit", name });
    out.push(...token);
    out.push({ type: "secret_text", name: "BRAIN_KEY", text: key });
    // The account id goes only to a Worker that holds a Cloudflare token: its cloudflareApi cell calls /accounts/ID.
    out.push({ type: "json", name: "BRAIN_CONFIG", json: { base: config.base, subdomain: config.subdomain, host: `${config.base}.${config.subdomain}.workers.dev`, owner: config.owner || null, deployer: `https://${selfScript()}.${config.subdomain}.workers.dev`, ...(token.length ? { account: config.account } : {}) } });
    out.push({
      type: "json",
      name: "BRAIN_INFO",
      json: { name: m.worker, hash: w.hash, role: m.role, module: m.module || null, methods: m.methods, access: m.access || {}, calls: m.calls || [], paths: m.paths, secrets: m.secrets, resources: m.resources, cloudflare: m.cloudflare || [], deployedAt: new Date().toISOString() }
    });
    return out;
  };

  const refusal = async (w, rec) => {
    const m = w.meta || {};
    const logical = m.worker;
    if (typeof logical !== "string" || !Array.isArray(m.resources) || !Array.isArray(m.secrets)) return "not an emitted Worker";
    if (logical === "brain-deployer" || logical === "brain-guard" || m.role === "deployer" || m.role === "guard") return 'resource name "brain-deployer" is reserved';
    // The table database is bound to one Worker, which checks every statement the others send it.
    if (m.resources.includes("database") && logical !== "brain-db") return "only brain-db is bound to the table database";
    const group = (m.cloudflare || []).find((g) => !GROUPS.includes(g));
    if ((m.cloudflare || []).length && m.role !== "recipe") return "only a recipe declares Cloudflare permissions";
    if (group) return `"${group}" is not a Cloudflare permission a service may declare. A service may declare: ${GROUPS.join(", ")}`;
    if (w.parts && (await partsHash(w.parts, m)) !== w.hash) return `the parts sent for "${logical}" do not hash to ${String(w.hash).slice(0, 12)}`;
    const tier = { kernel: "brain", core: "brain-core" }[m.role];
    if (tier) return tier === logical ? null : `role ${m.role} must be named ${tier}`;
    // A system Worker: routed by the core like a recipe, deployed like the core. Its name is not a recipe's.
    if (m.role === "system") return /^brain-(?!x-|m-|core$|deployer$|guard$)[a-z0-9-]+$/.test(logical) ? null : "role system must be named brain-NAME";
    if ((await rows.get("worker/" + logical.replace(/^brain-x-/, "brain-")) || {}).hash) return `${logical.replace(/^brain-x-/, "brain-")} is a system Worker`;
    const reason = deployerAllows({ key: "worker/" + logical, op: rec && rec.hash ? "update" : "create" });
    if (reason) return reason;
    // A method or path belongs to one Worker: the core routes to the Worker of the first service that declares it.
    for (const { value: other } of await rows.list("worker/")) {
      if (other.worker === logical || !other.hash) continue;
      const clash = (m.methods || []).find((x) => (other.methods || []).includes(x)) || (m.paths || []).map((x) => x.path).find((x) => (other.paths || []).some((o) => o.path === x));
      if (clash) return `${clash} is already served by ${other.worker}`;
    }
    const bad = m.resources.find((r) => !["rows", "blobs", "inbox", "xrpc", "assets", "sql", "browser"].includes(r));
    if (bad) return `a recipe may not use the platform cell "${bad}"`;
    return m.secrets.find((s) => s.startsWith("BRAIN_") || s.startsWith("CF_")) ? "a recipe may not name a BRAIN_ or CF_ secret" : null;
  };

  const register = async (rec, access) => {
    if (rec.role === "deployer" || rec.role === "guard") return;
    await toCore("service.register", {
      worker: rec.worker,
      role: rec.role,
      module: rec.module || null,
      hash: rec.hash,
      methods: access || {},
      author: rec.author || null,
      paths: rec.paths,
      secrets: rec.secrets,
      keyHash: await sha256(rec.key)
    });
    if (rec.role !== "recipe" && rec.role !== "system" && rec.role !== "member") return;
    const core = await rows.get("worker/brain-core");
    if (!core || !core.hash) return;
    const name = "X_" + rec.worker.replace(/^brain-(x-)?/, "").toUpperCase().replace(/[^A-Z0-9]/g, "_");
    const now = (await api("GET", script("brain-core") + "/settings")).bindings;
    if (now.some((b) => b.name === name)) return;
    const form = new FormData();
    form.append("settings", new Blob([text({ bindings: [...now.map((b) => ({ type: "inherit", name: b.name })), { type: "service", name, service: actual(rec.worker) }] })], { type: "application/json" }));
    await api("PATCH", script("brain-core") + "/settings", form);
    // The core now runs a version with one more binding and the same code: that version is the one to keep.
    const version = await currentVersion("brain-core");
    const ks = await rows.get("kernelstate/brain-core");
    if (ks && ks.state !== "probation") await rows.put("kernelstate/brain-core", { ...ks, version, lastGood: version });
    await rows.put("worker/brain-core", { ...core, version });
  };

  const deployOne = async (w, rec, given) => {
    const m = w.meta, logical = m.worker;
    const key = (rec && rec.key) || randomKey();
    const live = rec && rec.hash ? await api("GET", script(logical) + "/settings").catch(() => null) : null;
    const existing = new Set(live ? live.bindings.map((b) => b.name) : []);
    const token = await tokenFor(logical, [...(m.cloudflare || [])].sort(), existing);
    try {
      return await deployWith(w, rec, given, key, live, existing, token);
    } catch (e) {
      await token.undo();
      throw e;
    }
  };
  const deployWith = async (w, rec, given, key, live, existing, token) => {
    const m = w.meta, logical = m.worker;
    const bindings = await bindingsFor(w, key, existing, given, token.binding);
    const meta = { main_module: "worker.js", compatibility_date: "2026-10-01", compatibility_flags: [...new Set([...(m.flags || []), ...wrapperFlags])], observability: OBSERVABILITY, bindings };
    let assetHash = rec ? rec.assetHash : undefined;
    if (m.resources.includes("assets")) {
      if (typeof w.asset === "string") {
        const up = await uploadAsset(logical, w.asset);
        meta.assets = { jwt: up.jwt, config: { run_worker_first: true } };
        assetHash = up.hash;
      } else if (existing.has("ASSETS")) meta.keep_assets = true;
      else throw new Error(`"${logical}" needs its page and none was sent`);
    }
    const form = () => {
      const f = new FormData();
      f.append("metadata", new Blob([text(meta)], { type: "application/json" }));
      for (const p of w.parts) f.append(p.path, new File([p.text], p.path, { type: "application/javascript+module" }));
      return f;
    };
    const previous = live ? await currentVersion(logical) : null;
    let version;
    if (!live) {
      // A new script needs the script upload, which goes live at once.
      await api("PUT", script(logical), form());
      await api("POST", script(logical) + "/subdomain", text({ enabled: true }), jsonType);
      if (m.crons.length) await api("PUT", script(logical) + "/schedules", text(m.crons.map((cron) => ({ cron }))), jsonType);
      version = await currentVersion(logical);
      log({ at: "deploy.uploaded", target: logical, hash: w.hash, version, first: true });
      if (!(await waitHealthy(logical, key, w.hash))) {
        if (previous) await setVersions(logical, [{ version_id: previous, percentage: 100 }]);
        else await api("DELETE", script(logical) + "?force=true");
        throw new Error("health check failed after go-live");
      }
    } else {
      await ensureLogs(logical);
      version = (await api("POST", script(logical) + "/versions", form())).id;
      log({ at: "deploy.uploaded", target: logical, hash: w.hash, version, previous });
      await setVersions(logical, [{ version_id: previous, percentage: 100 }, { version_id: version, percentage: 0 }]);
      if (!(await waitHealthy(logical, key, w.hash, version))) {
        await setVersions(logical, [{ version_id: previous, percentage: 100 }]);
        throw new Error("self-test failed before go-live");
      }
      await setVersions(logical, [{ version_id: version, percentage: 100 }]);
      if (!(await waitHealthy(logical, key, w.hash))) {
        await setVersions(logical, [{ version_id: previous, percentage: 100 }]);
        throw new Error("health check failed after go-live");
      }
    }
    // What is needed to put the version before back, routes included.
    await token.done();
    const before = rec && rec.hash ? { hash: rec.hash, version: previous, module: rec.module, methods: rec.methods, access: rec.access, paths: rec.paths, secrets: rec.secrets, resources: rec.resources, cloudflare: rec.cloudflare || [], token: rec.token || null } : null;
    const next = {
      worker: logical, role: m.role, module: m.module || null, hash: w.hash, version, key, state: "deployed", fails: 0, assetHash, distiller: typeof w.source === "string" ? self.hash : null,
      previous: before,
      methods: m.methods, access: m.access || {}, paths: m.paths, secrets: m.secrets, resources: m.resources, cloudflare: m.cloudflare || [], token: token.id, deployedAt: Date.now()
    };
    await rows.put("worker/" + logical, next);
    await register(next, m.access);
    let state = "deployed";
    // The kernel, the core and the Worker the page comes from: a broken one cannot serve the page that would report
    // its tests, so these are also put back when nobody confirms in time.
    if (m.role !== "recipe" || (m.paths || []).some((p) => p.path === "/")) {
      if (previous) {
        await rows.put("kernelstate/" + logical, { state: "probation", version, lastGood: previous, since: Date.now(), fails: 0, hash: w.hash, lastGoodHash: rec.hash });
        state = "probation";
      } else {
        await rows.put("kernelstate/" + logical, { state: "confirmed", version, lastGood: version, hash: w.hash });
        await rows.put("confirmed/" + logical, [{ version, hash: w.hash, at: Date.now() }]);
      }
    }
    await note(`deploy/${logical}/${version}`, { event: state, worker: logical, hash: w.hash });
    log({ at: "deploy." + state, target: logical, hash: w.hash, version });
    return { state, version };
  };

  const apply = async ({ workers = [], remove = [], dry = false } = {}, { recovery = false } = {}) => {
    const approval = (await settings()).approval;
    const results = [];
    // A Worker given as source is distilled here, and what is deployed is what that gives. An import of another
    // module is answered from this apply first, then from the source of what is deployed.
    const sent = Object.fromEntries(workers.filter((w) => w && typeof w.source === "string" && typeof w.module === "string").map((w) => [w.module, w.source]));
    let kept;
    const distilled = [];
    for (const w of workers) {
      // Code made somewhere else is not deployed. config.acceptEmitted is set by this module's tests and by no installer.
      if (!w || typeof w.source !== "string") {
        if (config.acceptEmitted) distilled.push(w);
        else results.push({ worker: (w && w.meta && w.meta.worker) || (w && w.module) || null, state: "refused", reason: "send the module's source: this deployer deploys only what it distils" });
      } else
        try {
          kept ??= Object.fromEntries((await keptSources()).map((s) => [s.module, s.text]));
          const d = await deployerDistil({ module: w.module, source: w.source, cell: w.cell, files: w.files, sources: { ...kept, ...sent } });
          distilled.push({ ...w, parts: d.parts, meta: d.meta, hash: d.hash });
        } catch (e) {
          results.push({ worker: w.module, state: "refused", reason: "cannot distil: " + String((e && e.message) || e) });
        }
    }
    for (const w of distilled) {
      const logical = w && w.meta && w.meta.worker;
      const rec = typeof logical === "string" ? await rows.get("worker/" + logical) : null;
      const base = { worker: logical, hash: w && w.hash };
      const reason = await refusal(w || {}, rec);
      if (reason) results.push({ ...base, state: "refused", reason });
      else if (rec && rec.hash === w.hash && rec.state === "deployed" && !w.force && !(typeof w.asset === "string" && (await sha256(w.asset)).slice(0, 32) !== rec.assetHash)) {
        // Deployed before the deployer kept source: keep it now, since it is the source of what is running.
        if (typeof w.source === "string" && !(await rows.get("source/" + w.module))) await rows.put("source/" + w.module, { text: w.source, files: w.files || {}, cell: w.cell || null, worker: logical, hash: w.hash, at: Date.now(), prev: null });
        results.push({ ...base, state: "unchanged" });
      }
      // A service that declares Cloudflare permissions is held for the owner also when deploys need no approval.
      else if ((approval || (w.meta.cloudflare || []).length) && !recovery && !(await rows.get("approved/" + w.hash))) {
        const m = w.meta;
        await rows.put("pending/" + w.hash, { worker: logical, hash: w.hash, methods: m.methods, paths: m.paths, secrets: m.secrets, resources: m.resources, cloudflare: m.cloudflare || [], calls: m.calls || [], access: m.access || {}, at: Date.now() });
        results.push({ ...base, state: "waiting" });
      } else if (dry || !w.parts) results.push({ ...base, state: "ready" });
      else {
        try {
          // Only the installer, holding the recovery key, may hand a Worker a secret's value directly.
          results.push({ ...base, ...(await deployOne(w, rec, recovery && w.secrets ? w.secrets : {})) });
          if (typeof w.source === "string") {
            const was = await rows.get("source/" + w.module);
            const prev = was && !was.stale && was.worker === logical && was.hash !== w.hash ? { text: was.text, files: was.files, cell: was.cell, hash: was.hash, at: was.at } : (was && was.prev) || null;
            await rows.put("source/" + w.module, { text: w.source, files: w.files || {}, cell: w.cell || null, worker: logical, hash: w.hash, at: Date.now(), prev });
          }
        } catch (e) {
          const reason = String((e && e.message) || e);
          const kept = rec && rec.hash ? { ...rec, lastError: reason, lastErrorAt: Date.now(), failedHash: w.hash } : { worker: logical, role: w.meta.role, hash: null, key: rec && rec.key, state: "removed", lastError: reason, lastErrorAt: Date.now(), failedHash: w.hash };
          await rows.put("worker/" + logical, kept);
          await note(`put-back/${logical}/${w.hash}/${kept.lastErrorAt}`, { event: "put-back", worker: logical, hash: w.hash, previous: kept.hash, reason });
          log({ at: "deploy.put-back", target: logical, hash: w.hash, previous: kept.hash, reason });
          results.push({ ...base, state: "put-back", previous: kept.hash, reason });
        }
      }
    }
    for (const logical of remove) {
      const rec = await rows.get("worker/" + logical);
      const reason = deployerAllows({ key: "worker/" + logical, op: "delete" });
      if (reason) results.push({ worker: logical, state: "refused", reason });
      else if (approval && !recovery && !(await rows.get("approved/remove:" + logical))) {
        await rows.put("pending/remove:" + logical, { worker: logical, hash: "remove:" + logical, remove: true, at: Date.now() });
        results.push({ worker: logical, state: "waiting" });
      } else if (!dry) {
        await toCore("service.unregister", { worker: logical });
        const core = await rows.get("worker/brain-core");
        if (core && core.hash) {
          const name = "X_" + logical.slice("brain-x-".length).toUpperCase().replace(/[^A-Z0-9]/g, "_");
          const now = (await api("GET", script("brain-core") + "/settings")).bindings;
          if (now.some((b) => b.name === name)) {
            const form = new FormData();
            form.append("settings", new Blob([text({ bindings: now.filter((b) => b.name !== name).map((b) => ({ type: "inherit", name: b.name })) })], { type: "application/json" }));
            await api("PATCH", script("brain-core") + "/settings", form);
          }
        }
        if (rec && rec.hash) await api("DELETE", script(logical) + "?force=true");
        const token = await rows.get("token/" + logical);
        if (token) (await dropToken(logical, token), await rows.delete("token/" + logical));
        log({ at: "deploy.removed", target: logical, hash: rec && rec.hash });
        await rows.delete("worker/" + logical);
        await rows.delete("approved/remove:" + logical);
        results.push({ worker: logical, state: "removed" });
      } else results.push({ worker: logical, state: "ready" });
    }
    for (const r of results) if (r.state === "refused" || r.state === "waiting") log({ at: "deploy." + r.state, target: r.worker, hash: r.hash, reason: r.reason });
    return { results };
  };

  // Mints and binds the token of a Worker whose row says it declares groups and holds none. That makes one more
  // version with the same code. A failure is logged and the tick tries again.
  const remint = async (logical, rec) => {
    try {
      // A token left by a try that failed after it was bound: no Worker row names it, so it is ended here.
      const left = await rows.get("token/" + logical);
      if (left) (await rows.delete("token/" + logical), await dropToken(logical, left));
      const t = await mint(logical, rec.cloudflare), held = { id: t.id, groups: t.groups, expires: t.expires };
      try {
        const now = (await api("GET", script(logical) + "/settings")).bindings;
        const form = new FormData();
        form.append("settings", new Blob([text({ bindings: [...now.filter((b) => b.name !== "CF_TOKEN").map((b) => ({ type: "inherit", name: b.name })), { type: "secret_text", name: "CF_TOKEN", text: t.value }] })], { type: "application/json" }));
        await api("PATCH", script(logical) + "/settings", form);
      } catch (e) {
        await api("DELETE", "/tokens/" + t.id).catch(() => null);
        throw e;
      }
      await rows.put("token/" + logical, held);
      await audit("mint", logical, held);
      const next = { ...rec, token: t.id, version: await currentVersion(logical) };
      await rows.put("worker/" + logical, next);
      return next;
    } catch (e) {
      log({ at: "token.mint-failed", target: logical, reason: String((e && e.message) || e).slice(0, 300) });
      return rec;
    }
  };
  const putBack = async (logical, rec, to, reason) => {
    await setVersions(logical, [{ version_id: to.version, percentage: 100 }]);
    const at = Date.now();
    // The routes of the version put back, when they were kept: a deploy may have changed what the Worker answers.
    const old = rec.previous && rec.previous.version === to.version && rec.previous.methods ? rec.previous : {};
    const next = { ...rec, ...old, hash: to.hash, version: to.version, previous: null, fails: 0, state: "deployed", lastError: reason, lastErrorAt: at, failedHash: rec.hash };
    // The version put back holds the token value of its own deploy. When that is not the token held now, it was
    // deleted, and the Worker holds no token until remint gives it one.
    const groups = next.cloudflare || [];
    const stale = (groups.length || rec.token) && !("token" in old && old.token === (rec.token || null));
    if (stale) next.token = null;
    // The row first: what is live is recorded before a call to Cloudflare that can fail.
    log({ at: "deploy.put-back", target: logical, hash: rec.hash, previous: to.hash, reason });
    await rows.put("worker/" + logical, next);
    await sourcePutBack(logical, to.hash);
    await register(next, next.access).catch(() => null);
    await note(`put-back/${logical}/${rec.hash}/${at}`, { event: "put-back", worker: logical, hash: rec.hash, previous: to.hash, reason });
    if (!stale) return;
    const had = await rows.get("token/" + logical);
    if (had) (await rows.delete("token/" + logical), await dropToken(logical, had));
    if (groups.length) await remint(logical, next);
  };

  // The last run of the cron is recorded, so a deployer whose cron has stopped, or whose tick throws, can be seen.
  const tick = async () => {
    // A deployer that was replaced checks nothing and puts nothing back.
    if (config.replacedBy) return;
    const at = Date.now(), last = await rows.get("tick");
    // The cron and the alarm may both call within a minute; a check counts once.
    if (last && !last.error && at - last.at < (config.tickGapMs ?? 30000)) return;
    try {
      await runTick();
      await rows.put("tick", { at, ms: Date.now() - at });
    } catch (e) {
      await rows.put("tick", { at, error: String((e && e.message) || e) });
      throw e;
    }
  };
  const runTick = async () => {
    const onProbation = new Set();
    for (const { key, value: s } of await rows.list("kernelstate/")) {
      if (s.state !== "probation") continue;
      const logical = key.slice("kernelstate/".length);
      onProbation.add(logical);
      const rec = await rows.get("worker/" + logical);
      const next = nextKernelState(s, { type: "tick", now: Date.now(), healthy: await healthy(logical, rec.key), probationMs: config.probationMs });
      if (next.state === "rolled-back") await putBack(logical, rec, { version: s.lastGood, hash: s.lastGoodHash }, next.reason);
      await rows.put(key, next.state === "rolled-back" ? { ...next, hash: s.lastGoodHash, failedHash: s.hash, at: Date.now() } : next);
    }
    // Every other Worker: two failed checks in a row puts it back to the version before, when there is one.
    for (const row of await rows.list("worker/")) {
      let rec = row.value;
      if (rec.state !== "deployed" || !rec.hash || onProbation.has(rec.worker)) continue;
      // A Worker put back whose token could not be minted then. Its health is checked all the same.
      if ((rec.cloudflare || []).length && !rec.token) rec = await remint(rec.worker, rec);
      const fails = (await healthy(rec.worker, rec.key)) ? 0 : (rec.fails || 0) + 1;
      if (fails >= 2 && rec.previous) await putBack(rec.worker, rec, rec.previous, "health check failed twice");
      else if (fails !== (rec.fails || 0)) {
        await rows.put("worker/" + rec.worker, { ...rec, fails });
        if (fails === 2) (log({ at: "deploy.failing", target: rec.worker, hash: rec.hash, reason: "health check failed twice and there is no version before" }), await note(`failing/${rec.worker}/${rec.hash}`, { event: "failing", worker: rec.worker, hash: rec.hash }));
      }
    }
  };

  const confirm = async (only = null) => {
    const confirmed = [];
    for (const { key, value: s } of await rows.list("kernelstate/")) {
      if (s.state !== "probation") continue;
      const logical = key.slice("kernelstate/".length);
      if (only && logical !== only) continue;
      await rows.put(key, { ...nextKernelState(s, { type: "confirm" }), hash: s.hash });
      const list = (await rows.get("confirmed/" + logical)) || [];
      await rows.put("confirmed/" + logical, [{ version: s.version, hash: s.hash, at: Date.now() }, ...list].slice(0, 5));
      confirmed.push(logical);
      log({ at: "deploy.confirmed", target: logical, hash: s.hash, version: s.version });
    }
    return { confirmed };
  };

  const rollback = async (logical, version) => {
    const to = ((await rows.get("confirmed/" + logical)) || []).find((c) => c.version === version);
    if (!to) throw new Error(`${version} is not a confirmed version of ${logical}`);
    const rec = await rows.get("worker/" + logical);
    await putBack(logical, rec, to, "rolled back from the deployer page");
    await rows.put("kernelstate/" + logical, { state: "rolled-back", version, lastGood: version, hash: to.hash, reason: "rolled back from the deployer page", at: Date.now() });
  };

  // The core passes on what the page found when it ran a deployed module's tests.
  const verdict = async ({ worker: logical, hash, ok, reason = "" }) => {
    const rec = await rows.get("worker/" + logical);
    if (!rec || rec.hash !== hash) return { state: "stale" };
    const ks = await rows.get("kernelstate/" + logical);
    const probation = ks && ks.state === "probation";
    if (ok) {
      if (probation) await confirm(logical);
      return { state: "kept" };
    }
    const why = "its tests failed: " + String(reason).slice(0, 200);
    if (probation) {
      await putBack(logical, rec, { version: ks.lastGood, hash: ks.lastGoodHash }, why);
      await rows.put("kernelstate/" + logical, { state: "rolled-back", version: ks.lastGood, lastGood: ks.lastGood, hash: ks.lastGoodHash, failedHash: ks.hash, reason: why, at: Date.now() });
      return { state: "put-back", previous: ks.lastGoodHash };
    }
    if (!rec.previous) return { state: "kept", reason: "there is no version before this one" };
    const previous = rec.previous.hash;
    await putBack(logical, rec, rec.previous, why);
    return { state: "put-back", previous };
  };

  const approve = async (hash) => {
    const pending = await rows.get("pending/" + hash);
    if (!pending) return false;
    await rows.put("approved/" + hash, { at: Date.now(), worker: pending.worker });
    await rows.delete("pending/" + hash);
    return true;
  };

  const state = async () => ({
    base: config.base,
    replacedBy: config.replacedBy || null,
    approval: (await settings()).approval,
    tick: await rows.get("tick"),
    workers: (await rows.list("worker/")).map(({ value: { key, ...rest } }) => rest),
    kernel: Object.fromEntries(
      (await rows.list("kernelstate/")).map(({ key, value }) => [
        key.slice("kernelstate/".length),
        value.state === "probation" ? { ...value, deadline: value.since + (config.probationMs ?? 10 * 60 * 1000) } : value
      ])
    ),
    confirmed: Object.fromEntries((await rows.list("confirmed/")).map(({ key, value }) => [key.slice("confirmed/".length), value])),
    pending: (await rows.list("pending/")).map((r) => r.value),
    // The deployer answering, and the deployer that last distilled everything. Different: redistil has not run since an update.
    distiller: { now: self.hash, last: await rows.get("distiller") },
    approved: (await rows.list("approved/")).map((r) => r.key.slice("approved/".length))
  });

  const setApproval = async (on) => rows.put("settings", { ...(await settings()), approval: !!on });

  // Distils the kept source of every running Worker again with this deployer. One whose code comes out different is
  // listed, and deployed when asked, by the same path as any deploy. Run after the deployer is updated.
  const redistil = async ({ apply: go = false } = {}, { recovery = false } = {}) => {
    const kept = await keptSources();
    const sources = Object.fromEntries(kept.map((s) => [s.module, s.text]));
    const results = [], changed = [];
    for (const s of kept) {
      const rec = await rows.get("worker/" + s.worker);
      if (!rec || !rec.hash) continue;
      const base = { worker: s.worker, module: s.module };
      if (rec.hash !== s.hash) {
        results.push({ ...base, state: "no source", reason: `${String(rec.hash).slice(0, 12)} is running and the source kept is of ${String(s.hash).slice(0, 12)}` });
        continue;
      }
      try {
        const d = await deployerDistil({ module: s.module, source: s.text, cell: s.cell || undefined, files: s.files, sources });
        if (d.hash === rec.hash) {
          results.push({ ...base, state: "same", hash: d.hash });
          if (rec.distiller !== self.hash) await rows.put("worker/" + s.worker, { ...rec, distiller: self.hash });
        } else {
          results.push({ ...base, state: "changes", from: rec.hash, hash: d.hash });
          changed.push({ module: s.module, source: s.text, cell: s.cell || undefined, files: s.files });
        }
      } catch (e) {
        results.push({ ...base, state: "cannot distil", reason: String((e && e.message) || e) });
      }
    }
    if (go && changed.length) {
      const out = await apply({ workers: changed }, { recovery });
      for (const r of out.results) {
        const row = results.find((x) => x.worker === r.worker && x.state === "changes");
        if (row) Object.assign(row, { applied: r.state }, r.reason ? { reason: r.reason } : {});
      }
    }
    const held = new Set(kept.map((s) => s.worker));
    // A script deployed before 2026-10-08 keeps no logs until this is set: each one, a member's and one with no source too.
    for (const { value: rec } of await rows.list("worker/")) if (rec.hash) await ensureLogs(rec.worker).catch(() => null);
    for (const { value: rec } of await rows.list("worker/")) if (rec.hash && rec.role !== "member" && !held.has(rec.worker)) results.push({ worker: rec.worker, module: rec.module || null, state: "no source", reason: "deployed before the deployer kept source" });
    await rows.put("distiller", { hash: self.hash, at: Date.now(), results: results.map(({ worker, state, applied }) => ({ worker, state, applied })) });
    return { distiller: self.hash, results };
  };

  // A member's Worker. The deployer takes nothing from what was distilled but its code: the name, the bindings, the
  // methods and their rules are made here. It is bound to the core and to nothing else, has no address on the
  // internet, and is deployed with no approval.
  const MEMBER = { workers: 3, partBytes: 1000000, sourceChars: 200000 };
  const memberId = async (did) => (await sha256(did)).slice(0, 10);
  const dropCoreBinding = async (logical) => {
    const core = await rows.get("worker/brain-core");
    if (!core || !core.hash) return;
    const name = "X_" + logical.replace(/^brain-(x-)?/, "").toUpperCase().replace(/[^A-Z0-9]/g, "_");
    const now = (await api("GET", script("brain-core") + "/settings")).bindings;
    if (!now.some((b) => b.name === name)) return;
    const form = new FormData();
    form.append("settings", new Blob([text({ bindings: now.filter((b) => b.name !== name).map((b) => ({ type: "inherit", name: b.name })) })], { type: "application/json" }));
    await api("PATCH", script("brain-core") + "/settings", form);
  };
  const memberRemoveOne = async (logical) => {
    const rec = await rows.get("worker/" + logical);
    await toCore("service.unregister", { worker: logical });
    await dropCoreBinding(logical);
    if (rec && rec.hash) await api("DELETE", script(logical) + "?force=true").catch(() => null);
    await rows.delete("worker/" + logical);
    await rows.delete("msource/" + logical);
  };
  const memberDeploy = async ({ author, quota = {}, request = {} } = {}) => {
    const refuse = (reason, worker = null) => ({ worker, state: "refused", reason });
    if (typeof author !== "string" || !author.startsWith("did:") || author === config.owner) return refuse("a member");
    const id = await memberId(author), ns = `com.lopecode.brain.m.${id}.`;
    let d;
    if (typeof request.source === "string" && typeof request.module === "string") {
      if (request.source.length > MEMBER.sourceChars) return refuse(`the source is over ${MEMBER.sourceChars} characters`);
      try {
        // Distilled alone: an import is answered by cloudflare-iac and by nothing kept from another Worker.
        d = await deployerDistil({ module: request.module, source: request.source, cell: request.cell, files: {}, sources: {} });
      } catch (e) {
        return refuse("cannot distil: " + String((e && e.message) || e));
      }
    } else if (config.acceptEmitted && request.parts) d = request;
    else return refuse("send module and source: this deployer deploys only what it distils");
    const m = d.meta || {};
    const short = String(m.worker || "").replace(/^brain-x-/, "");
    if (m.role !== "recipe" || !/^[a-z0-9]{1,20}$/.test(short)) return refuse('a member service is cloudflare.Service("NAME", …): NAME is 1 to 20 lower case letters and digits, with no role');
    const logical = `brain-m-${id}-${short}`;
    const bad = (m.resources || []).find((r) => !["sql", "xrpc"].includes(r));
    if (bad) return refuse(`a member service may not use the platform cell "${bad}"`, logical);
    if ((m.secrets || []).length) return refuse("a member service may not name a secret", logical);
    if ((m.cloudflare || []).length) return refuse("a member service may not declare Cloudflare permissions", logical);
    if ((m.paths || []).length) return refuse("a member service has no paths", logical);
    if ((m.crons || []).length || (m.flags || []).length) return refuse("a member service has no schedule and no flags", logical);
    const access = {};
    for (const [nsid, rule] of Object.entries(m.access || {})) {
      if (!nsid.startsWith(ns) || !/^[A-Za-z0-9.]{1,60}$/.test(nsid.slice(ns.length))) return refuse(`${nsid}: a method of this member is named ${ns}NAME`, logical);
      if (!rule || rule.allow || !["author", "members"].includes(rule.who)) return refuse(`${nsid}: who is "author" or "members"`, logical);
      access[nsid] = { type: rule.type === "query" ? "query" : "procedure", who: rule.who, allow: rule.who === "author" ? `caller.kind == "owner" || caller.did == ${JSON.stringify(author)}` : 'caller.kind in ["owner", "did"]' };
    }
    const parts = d.parts || [];
    if (!parts.length || parts.some((p) => typeof p.text !== "string" || !/^(worker\.js|source\.js|lib\/[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\.js)$/.test(p.path))) return refuse("the parts are worker.js, source.js and lib/NAME.js", logical);
    const size = parts.reduce((n, p) => n + p.text.length, 0);
    if (size > MEMBER.partBytes) return refuse(`${size} characters of code, at most ${MEMBER.partBytes}`, logical);
    const rec = await rows.get("worker/" + logical);
    const mine = (await rows.list(`worker/brain-m-${id}-`)).filter((r) => r.value.hash).length;
    const limit = Number.isFinite(quota.workers) ? quota.workers : MEMBER.workers;
    if (!(rec && rec.hash) && mine >= limit) return refuse(`${mine} services are deployed, at most ${limit}`, logical);
    const methods = Object.keys(access).sort();
    for (const { value: other } of await rows.list("worker/")) {
      const clash = other.worker !== logical && other.hash && methods.find((x) => (other.methods || []).includes(x));
      if (clash) return refuse(`${clash} is already served by ${other.worker}`, logical);
    }
    const meta = { worker: logical, role: "member", author, module: m.module || request.module || null, calls: [], crons: [], flags: [], methods, access, paths: [], secrets: [], resources: [...(m.resources || [])].sort(), bindings: [] };
    const hash = await partsHash(parts, meta);
    if (rec && rec.hash === hash && rec.state === "deployed") return { worker: logical, hash, state: "unchanged", methods };
    const key = (rec && rec.key) || randomKey();
    const live = rec && rec.hash ? await api("GET", script(logical) + "/settings").catch(() => null) : null;
    const form = new FormData();
    form.append("metadata", new Blob([text({
      main_module: "worker.js", compatibility_date: "2026-10-01", compatibility_flags: [...wrapperFlags], observability: OBSERVABILITY,
      bindings: [
        { type: "service", name: "CORE", service: actual("brain-core") },
        { type: "secret_text", name: "BRAIN_KEY", text: key },
        { type: "json", name: "BRAIN_CONFIG", json: { base: config.base, host: `${config.base}.${config.subdomain}.workers.dev` } },
        { type: "json", name: "BRAIN_INFO", json: { name: logical, hash, role: "member", author, module: meta.module, methods, access, calls: [], paths: [], secrets: [], resources: meta.resources, deployedAt: new Date().toISOString() } }
      ]
    })], { type: "application/json" }));
    for (const p of parts) form.append(p.path, new File([p.text], p.path, { type: "application/javascript+module" }));
    const previous = live ? await currentVersion(logical) : null;
    try {
      await api("PUT", script(logical), form);
      if (!live) await api("POST", script(logical) + "/subdomain", text({ enabled: false, previews_enabled: false }), jsonType);
      const version = await currentVersion(logical);
      const next = {
        worker: logical, role: "member", author, module: meta.module, hash, version, key, state: "deployed", fails: 0,
        previous: rec && rec.hash ? { hash: rec.hash, version: previous, module: rec.module, methods: rec.methods, access: rec.access, paths: [], secrets: [], resources: rec.resources } : null,
        methods, access, paths: [], secrets: [], resources: meta.resources, deployedAt: Date.now()
      };
      await rows.put("worker/" + logical, next);
      await register(next, access);
      if (!(await waitHealthy(logical, key, hash))) throw new Error("health check failed after go-live");
      await ensureLogs(logical).catch(() => null);
      log({ at: "deploy.deployed", target: logical, hash, version, previous: (rec && rec.hash) || null });
      await rows.put("msource/" + logical, { module: meta.module, text: typeof request.source === "string" ? request.source : null, author, hash, at: Date.now() });
      await note(`deploy/${logical}/${version}`, { event: "deployed", worker: logical, hash, author });
      return { worker: logical, hash, state: "deployed", methods };
    } catch (e) {
      const reason = String((e && e.message) || e);
      if (rec && rec.hash && previous) {
        await setVersions(logical, [{ version_id: previous, percentage: 100 }]).catch(() => null);
        await rows.put("worker/" + logical, { ...rec, lastError: reason, lastErrorAt: Date.now(), failedHash: hash });
        await register(rec, rec.access).catch(() => null);
      } else await memberRemoveOne(logical).catch(() => null);
      log({ at: "deploy.put-back", target: logical, hash, previous: (rec && rec.hash) || null, reason });
      return { worker: logical, hash, state: "put-back", previous: (rec && rec.hash) || null, reason };
    }
  };
  const memberRemove = async ({ author, request = {} } = {}) => {
    const logical = `brain-m-${await memberId(String(author))}-${String(request.name || "")}`;
    const rec = await rows.get("worker/" + logical);
    if (!rec || rec.author !== author) return { worker: logical, state: "refused", reason: "not a service of this member" };
    await memberRemoveOne(logical);
    return { worker: logical, state: "removed" };
  };
  // Every Worker of one member, when the owner removes them.
  const memberPurge = async ({ author } = {}) => {
    const removed = [];
    for (const { value: rec } of await rows.list(`worker/brain-m-${await memberId(String(author))}-`)) {
      if (rec.author !== author) continue;
      await memberRemoveOne(rec.worker);
      removed.push(rec.worker);
    }
    return { removed };
  };

  // Moving to a new Worker name. A new name is a new Worker with no rows. exportRows gives every row of this
  // deployer, the key of each Worker included; importRows takes them into a deployer that holds none. tick and
  // distiller are this deployer's own notes and are not counted. rowsDigest is what both sides compare: per class of
  // row, how many and the SHA-256 of their keys and values.
  const OWN = new Set(["tick", "distiller"]);
  const exportRows = async () => ({ rows: (await rows.list("")).filter((r) => !OWN.has(r.key)) });
  const rowsDigest = async () => {
    const classes = {};
    for (const r of (await rows.list("")).filter((x) => !OWN.has(x.key)).sort((a, b) => (a.key < b.key ? -1 : 1))) {
      const c = (classes[r.key.split("/")[0]] ??= { rows: 0, text: "" });
      c.rows++;
      c.text = await sha256(c.text + "\n" + r.key + "\n" + JSON.stringify(r.value));
    }
    return { classes: Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(classes).map(([k, v]) => [k, { rows: v.rows, sha256: v.text }])) };
  };
  const importRows = async ({ rows: given } = {}) => {
    if (!Array.isArray(given) || given.some((r) => !r || typeof r.key !== "string" || r.key.startsWith("__"))) return { error: "InvalidRequest", message: "rows: [{ key, value }]" };
    const held = (await rows.list("")).filter((r) => !OWN.has(r.key)).length;
    if (held) return { error: "NotEmpty", message: `this deployer holds ${held} rows; rows are imported into a deployer that holds none` };
    for (const r of given) if (!OWN.has(r.key)) await rows.put(r.key, r.value);
    return { imported: given.filter((r) => !OWN.has(r.key)).length, ...(await rowsDigest()) };
  };

  return { apply, tick, confirm, rollback, approve, state, setApproval, verdict, shell, redistil, self, memberDeploy, memberRemove, memberPurge, memberId, exportRows, importRows, rowsDigest };
}
// %%
md`## The page

\`https://BASE-deployer.SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev/\`. One HTML response, no script. The status lines are public; every action needs the recovery key.`
// %%
deployerPage = (s, message = "") => {
  const esc = (v) => String(v ?? "").replace(/[&<>"]/g, (c) => ({ "&": "&amp;", "<": "&lt;", ">": "&gt;", '"': "&quot;" }[c]));
  const short = (h) => esc(String(h || "none").slice(0, 12));
  const when = (t) => (t ? new Date(t).toISOString().slice(0, 16).replace("T", " ") + " UTC" : "");
  const worker = (w) =>
    `<tr><td>${esc(w.worker)}</td><td><code>${short(w.hash)}</code></td><td>${esc(w.state)}${w.fails >= 2 ? ", failing" : ""}</td><td>${w.lastError ? esc(w.lastError) + " (" + when(w.lastErrorAt) + ")" : ""}</td></tr>`;
  const kernel = Object.entries(s.kernel).map(([name, k]) =>
    k.state === "probation"
      ? `<p class="amber">${esc(name)} <code>${short(k.hash)}</code> is on probation until ${when(k.deadline)}.</p>`
      : k.state === "rolled-back"
      ? `<p class="red">${esc(name)} was rolled back to <code>${short(k.hash)}</code> at ${when(k.at)}: ${esc(k.reason)}</p>`
      : `<p>${esc(name)} <code>${short(k.hash)}</code> is confirmed.</p>`
  );
  // What the owner approves: the methods and paths a Worker answers and who may call each, the methods of other
  // Workers it calls, and the secrets it names. A rule that reads origin is marked: it limits who a Worker may act for.
  const nsid = (n) => esc(String(n).replace("com.lopecode.brain.", ""));
  const rule = (r) => (r && r.allow ? `<code>${esc(typeof r.allow === "string" ? r.allow : r.allow.source || JSON.stringify(r.allow))}</code>${/\borigin\b/.test(JSON.stringify(r.allow)) ? " (reads origin)" : ""}` : esc((r && r.who) || "owner")) + (r && r.price ? ` Price in USD: <code>${esc(String(r.price))}</code>` : "");
  const pending = s.pending.map((p) => {
    const answers = [
      // A deploy held before 2026-10-07 has no rules in its record.
      ...(p.methods || []).map((m) => `<tr><td>${nsid(m)}</td><td>${p.access ? rule(p.access[m]) : "not recorded"}</td></tr>`),
      ...(p.paths || []).map((x) => `<tr><td>${esc(x.path)}</td><td>${rule(x)}</td></tr>`)
    ];
    return `<li><b>${esc(p.worker)}</b> <code>${short(p.hash)}</code>${p.remove ? " (remove)" : ""} <button name="action" value="approve:${esc(p.hash)}">Approve</button>${
      p.remove
        ? ""
        : `<table><tr><th>Answers</th><th>Who may call</th></tr>${answers.join("") || "<tr><td>nothing</td><td></td></tr>"}</table>
<p>Calls: ${p.calls ? (p.calls.length ? p.calls.map(nsid).join(", ") : "none") : "not recorded"}. Secrets: ${esc((p.secrets || []).join(", ") || "none")}.</p>${
            (p.resources || []).includes("browser") ? "<p><b>Opens remote browsers.</b> Cloudflare bills browser time to this account.</p>" : ""
          }${(p.cloudflare || []).length ? `<p><b>Cloudflare permissions: ${esc(p.cloudflare.join(", "))}.</b> The deployer mints a Cloudflare API token with these and gives it to this Worker.</p>` : ""}`
    }</li>`;
  });
  const rollbacks = Object.entries(s.confirmed).flatMap(([name, list]) =>
    list.map((c) => `<button name="action" value="rollback:${esc(name)}:${esc(c.version)}">Roll back ${esc(name)} to ${short(c.hash)} (${when(c.at)})</button>`)
  );
  return `<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Cloud Brain deployer</title><style>
body{font:15px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:720px;margin:2rem auto;padding:0 1rem;color:#111;background:#fff}
table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{text-align:left;padding:.25rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;vertical-align:top}
button{font:inherit;margin:.2rem .3rem .2rem 0;padding:.3rem .6rem}input{font:inherit;padding:.3rem;width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}
.amber{color:#8a6300}.red{color:#b3261e}.note{background:#f2f2f2;padding:.5rem .75rem}</style></head><body>
<h1>Cloud Brain deployer</h1>
${message ? `<p class="note">${esc(message)}</p>` : ""}
${s.replacedBy ? `<p class="red">This deployer was replaced. The deployer of this Brain is at <a href="${esc(s.replacedBy)}">${esc(s.replacedBy)}</a>.</p>` : ""}
<p>Brain <code>${esc(s.base)}</code>. ${s.kernel.brain ? "" : "No kernel is deployed."}</p>
${kernel.join("\n")}
<table><tr><th>Worker</th><th>Hash</th><th>State</th><th>Last error</th></tr>${s.workers.map(worker).join("")}</table>
<form method="post" action="/">
${s.distiller && s.distiller.now && (!s.distiller.last || s.distiller.last.hash !== s.distiller.now) ? `<p class="amber">This deployer <code>${short(s.distiller.now)}</code> has not distilled the Workers again since it was updated.</p>` : ""}
<h2>Waiting for approval</h2>
${pending.length ? `<ul>${pending.join("")}</ul>` : "<p>Nothing is waiting.</p>"}
<h2>Roll back</h2>
${rollbacks.length ? rollbacks.join("<br>") : "<p>No confirmed version to roll back to.</p>"}
<h2>Deploys need approval: ${s.approval ? "on" : "off"}</h2>
<button name="action" value="approval:${s.approval ? "off" : "on"}">Turn ${s.approval ? "off" : "on"}</button>
<h2><label for="key">Recovery key</label></h2>
<input id="key" name="key" type="password" autocomplete="off" required>
</form></body></html>`;
}
// %%
deployerFn = async (request, context) => {
  const url = new URL(request.url);
  deployerOps.self.hash = (context && context.info && context.info.hash) || null;
  const cors = { "access-control-allow-origin": "*", "access-control-allow-headers": "content-type, authorization", "access-control-allow-methods": "GET, POST" };
  const json = (value, status = 200) => new Response(JSON.stringify(value), { status, headers: { "content-type": "application/json", ...cors } });
  const page = async (message, status = 200) =>
    new Response(deployerPage(await deployerOps.state(), message), { status, headers: { "content-type": "text/html; charset=utf-8", "cache-control": "no-store" } });
  if (request.method === "OPTIONS") return new Response(null, { headers: cors });
  const inside = url.hostname.endsWith(".internal");
  const recoveryKey = await secrets.RECOVERY_KEY;
  // For anyone: the source of every module a Worker of this Brain owns, as the deployer holds it. A page with no
  // service modules of its own loads them from here. Source is public at each Worker's getSource already.
  if (url.pathname === "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.infra.getModules" && request.method === "GET" && !inside)
    return json({ distiller: deployerOps.self.hash, modules: await deployerModules(context && context.source) });
  // A member's own deploys, passed on by the kernel with the DID it signed in. No approval and no recovery key.
  if (url.pathname.startsWith("/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.member.") && request.method === "POST") {
    const kernel = await rows.get("worker/brain");
    if (!(inside && !!kernel && !!kernel.key && request.headers.get("x-brain-key") === kernel.key)) return json({ error: "AuthRequired", message: "the kernel" }, 401);
    if (config.replacedBy) return json({ error: "Replaced", message: "this deployer was replaced by " + config.replacedBy, deployer: config.replacedBy }, 409);
    const method = url.pathname.slice("/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.member.".length), caller = request.headers.get("x-brain-caller"), body = await request.json().catch(() => ({}));
    if (method === "deploy" && caller === "member") return json(await deployerOps.memberDeploy(body));
    if (method === "remove" && caller === "member") return json(await deployerOps.memberRemove(body));
    // A member's own modules and cloudflare-iac: what a page served to that member would load.
    if (method === "modules" && caller === "member") return json({ distiller: deployerOps.self.hash, modules: await deployerModules(null, body.author) });
    if (method === "purge" && caller === "owner") return json(await deployerOps.memberPurge(body));
    return json({ error: "MethodNotImplemented", message: method }, 501);
  }
  if (url.pathname.startsWith("/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.infra.")) {
    // Two callers: the kernel over its binding, for the signed-in owner; or the holder of the recovery key.
    const kernel = await rows.get("worker/brain");
    const viaKernel = inside && !!kernel && !!kernel.key && request.headers.get("x-brain-key") === kernel.key && request.headers.get("x-brain-caller") === "owner";
    const recovery = !inside && !!recoveryKey && request.headers.get("authorization") === "Bearer " + recoveryKey;
    const method = url.pathname.slice("/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.infra.".length);
    // A third caller, for one method: the core, passing on the page's verdict on a deploy.
    const coreRec = await rows.get("worker/brain-core");
    if (method === "verdict" && request.method === "POST" && inside && !!coreRec && !!coreRec.key && request.headers.get("x-brain-key") === coreRec.key) return json(await deployerOps.verdict(await request.json()));
    if (!viaKernel && !recovery) return json({ error: "AuthRequired", message: "the owner's session or the recovery key" }, 401);
    // The rows hold every Worker's key: they leave and enter with the recovery key only, never through the kernel.
    if (["exportRows", "importRows", "rowsDigest"].includes(method)) {
      if (!recovery) return json({ error: "AuthRequired", message: "the recovery key" }, 401);
      if (method === "rowsDigest" && request.method === "GET") return json(await deployerOps.rowsDigest());
      if (method === "exportRows" && request.method === "GET") return json(await deployerOps.exportRows());
      if (method === "importRows" && request.method === "POST") {
        const out = await deployerOps.importRows(await request.json().catch(() => ({})));
        return json(out, out.error === "NotEmpty" ? 409 : out.error ? 400 : 200);
      }
      return json({ error: "MethodNotImplemented", message: method }, 501);
    }
    // A deployer that was replaced changes nothing. It still answers getState and exportRows.
    if (config.replacedBy && request.method === "POST") return json({ error: "Replaced", message: "this deployer was replaced by " + config.replacedBy, deployer: config.replacedBy }, 409);
    if (method === "getState" && request.method === "GET") return json(await deployerOps.state());
    if (method === "apply" && request.method === "POST") return json(await deployerOps.apply(await request.json(), { recovery }));
    if (method === "confirm" && request.method === "POST") return json(await deployerOps.confirm());
    // An installer's shell, passed on to brain-static as it arrives. The deployer keeps none of it.
    if (method === "shell" && request.method === "POST") return deployerOps.shell(request);
    if (method === "redistil" && request.method === "POST") return json(await deployerOps.redistil(await request.json().catch(() => ({})), { recovery }));
    // Answers what a source distils to. Deploys nothing.
    if (method === "distil" && request.method === "POST") {
      try {
        return json(await deployerDistil(await request.json()));
      } catch (e) {
        return json({ error: "InvalidRequest", message: String((e && e.message) || e) }, 400);
      }
    }
    if (method === "verdict") return json({ error: "AuthRequired", message: "the core" }, 401);
    return json({ error: "MethodNotImplemented", message: method }, 501);
  }
  if (inside || url.pathname !== "/") return new Response("not found", { status: 404 });
  if (request.method === "GET") return page();
  if (request.method !== "POST") return new Response("method not allowed", { status: 405 });
  if (config.replacedBy) return page("This deployer was replaced by " + config.replacedBy + ". Nothing was changed.", 409);
  const form = await request.formData();
  if (!recoveryKey || form.get("key") !== recoveryKey) return page("Wrong recovery key. Nothing was changed.", 401);
  const [action, a, b] = String(form.get("action") || "").split(":");
  try {
    if (action === "approve") return page((await deployerOps.approve(a === "remove" ? "remove:" + b : a)) ? "Approved. Press Apply in the Brain again." : "Nothing with that hash is waiting.");
    if (action === "rollback") return await deployerOps.rollback(a, b), page(`Rolled ${a} back.`);
    if (action === "approval") return await deployerOps.setApproval(a === "on"), page(`Deploys need approval: ${a === "on" ? "on" : "off"}.`);
    return page("Unknown action.", 400);
  } catch (e) {
    return page("Failed: " + String((e && e.message) || e), 500);
  }
}
// %%
// cloudflare-iac and this module are the deployer's own; every other module is the kept source of a running Worker.
deployerModules = async (own, member = null) => {
  const d = distillerData.default, IAC = "@tomlarkworthy/cloudflare-iac";
  const files = { ...(d.files || {}) };
  for (const [id, text] of Object.entries(d.content)) if (id.startsWith(IAC + "/")) files[id.slice(IAC.length + 1)] = text;
  for (const [from, name] of [["observable-runtime", "observable-runtime.js"], ["acorn", "acorn.js"], ["acorn-walk", "acorn-walk.js"]]) files[name] = d.modules[from];
  const out = [{ module: IAC, worker: "brain-deployer", hash: deployerOps.self.hash, text: d.modules[IAC], files }];
  // For one member (member.modules): their own services and cloudflare-iac. The list for anyone holds no member's
  // module: the Brain's page runs as whoever is signed in, the owner included.
  if (member) {
    for (const { key, value } of await rows.list(`msource/brain-m-${await deployerOps.memberId(member)}-`)) if (value.text) out.push({ module: value.module, worker: key.slice("msource/".length), hash: value.hash, text: value.text, files: {} });
    return out;
  }
  if (own && own.text) out.push({ module: own.module, worker: "brain-deployer", hash: deployerOps.self.hash, text: own.text, files: {} });
  for (const { key, value } of await rows.list("source/")) if (!value.stale) out.push({ module: key.slice("source/".length), worker: value.worker, hash: value.hash, text: value.text, files: value.files || {} });
  return out;
}
// %%
deployerDistil = async (request) => {
  if (!request || typeof request.module !== "string" || typeof request.source !== "string") throw new Error("module and source are required");
  return distilIn(async () => quickjsLib.load(await quickjs.module()), distillerData.default, request);
}
// %%
md`## Tests

The deployer runs under \`simulate\` against \`fakeCloudflare\`, a stand-in for the Cloudflare API and for the Workers it deploys. A hash added to \`fake.unhealthy\` makes that version fail its health check.`
// %%
fakeCloudflare = () => {
  const scripts = new Map(), log = [], calls = [], unhealthy = new Set(), stored = {}, d1 = [], tokens = new Map();
  const account = ["com.cloudflare.api.account"];
  const groups = [
    { id: "g-obs-user", name: "Workers Observability Read", scopes: ["com.cloudflare.api.user"] },
    { id: "g-obs", name: "Workers Observability Read", scopes: account },
    { id: "g-tail", name: "Workers Tail Read", scopes: account },
    { id: "g-scripts", name: "Workers Scripts Write", scopes: account }
  ];
  let n = 0;
  const ok = (result) => new Response(JSON.stringify({ success: true, result }), { headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
  const bad = (status, message) => new Response(JSON.stringify({ success: false, errors: [{ message }] }), { status });
  const bindingOf = (v, name) => v.metadata.bindings.find((b) => b.name === name);
  const live = (s) => s.versions.get(s.deployment.find((d) => d.percentage === 100).version_id);
  const resolve = (s, bindings) =>
    bindings.map((b) => {
      if (b.type !== "inherit") return b;
      const from = s && live(s).metadata.bindings.find((p) => p.name === b.name);
      if (!from) throw new Error("inherit of a binding that does not exist: " + b.name);
      return from;
    });
  const version = async (s, request) => {
    const form = await request.formData();
    const metadata = JSON.parse(await form.get("metadata").text());
    metadata.bindings = resolve(s, metadata.bindings);
    const id = "v" + ++n;
    return { id, metadata, parts: [...form.keys()].filter((k) => k !== "metadata") };
  };
  const fetch = async (request) => {
    const url = new URL(request.url);
    log.push(request.method + " " + url.hostname.split(".")[0] + url.pathname.replace("/client/v4/accounts/acct", ""));
    if (url.hostname.endsWith(".workers.dev")) {
      const s = scripts.get(url.hostname.split(".")[0]);
      if (!s) return new Response("no such script", { status: 404 });
      const over = /="([^"]+)"/.exec(request.headers.get("Cloudflare-Workers-Version-Overrides") || "");
      const v = over && s.deployment.some((d) => d.version_id === over[1]) ? s.versions.get(over[1]) : live(s);
      // The deployer sends the key under both names: a Worker deployed before 2026-10-08 reads x-brain-guard.
      if (request.headers.get("x-brain-deployer") !== bindingOf(v, "BRAIN_KEY").text || request.headers.get("x-brain-guard") !== bindingOf(v, "BRAIN_KEY").text) return new Response("not found", { status: 404 });
      const info = bindingOf(v, "BRAIN_INFO").json;
      if (url.pathname === "/xrpc/_health")
        return unhealthy.has(info.hash) ? new Response("broken", { status: 500 }) : Response.json({ ok: true, name: info.name, hash: info.hash });
      const sent = request.method === "POST" ? await request.text() : null;
      let body = sent;
      try {
        body = sent == null ? null : JSON.parse(sent);
      } catch {}
      calls.push({ worker: info.name, nsid: url.pathname.replace("/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.", ""), body, query: url.search });
      if (url.pathname.endsWith(".service.health")) {
        const m = scripts.get("cb" + body.worker.slice("brain".length));
        const h = m ? bindingOf(live(m), "BRAIN_INFO").json.hash : null;
        return Response.json({ ok: !!m && !unhealthy.has(h), hash: h });
      }
      return Response.json({});
    }
    if (request.headers.get("authorization") !== "Bearer tok" && !url.pathname.endsWith("/assets/upload")) return bad(403, "bad token");
    const path = url.pathname.replace("/client/v4/accounts/acct", "");
    if (path === "/workers/assets/upload") return ok({ jwt: "asset-done" });
    if (path === "/r2/buckets") return ok({});
    // One D1 database per Brain: found by name, made once.
    if (path.startsWith("/d1/database")) {
      if (request.method === "GET") return ok(d1);
      d1.push({ name: JSON.parse(await request.text()).name, uuid: "d1-" + (d1.length + 1) });
      return ok(d1.at(-1));
    }
    // Account tokens: the value is given once, at the mint.
    if (path === "/tokens/permission_groups") return ok(groups);
    if (path === "/tokens" && request.method === "POST") {
      if (stored.noMint) return bad(403, "minting is refused");
      const id = "t" + log.length, body = await request.json();
      tokens.set(id, { id, ...body, status: "active", value: "minted-" + id });
      return ok({ id, value: "minted-" + id, status: "active" });
    }
    const t = /^\/tokens\/([^/]+)$/.exec(path);
    if (t && !tokens.has(t[1])) return bad(404, "no token " + t[1]);
    if (t && request.method === "GET") return ok({ id: t[1], status: "active" });
    if (t && request.method === "DELETE") return tokens.delete(t[1]), ok({ id: t[1] });
    const m = /^\/workers\/scripts\/([^/]+)(\/.*)?$/.exec(path);
    if (!m) return bad(404, "no route " + path);
    const name = m[1], rest = m[2] || "", s = scripts.get(name);
    if (rest === "/assets-upload-session") return ok({ jwt: "asset-session", buckets: [["h"]] });
    if (rest === "" && request.method === "PUT") {
      const v = await version(s, request);
      const next = s || { versions: new Map(), deployment: [], schedules: [], subdomain: false };
      // The script's own settings: taken from the upload of a script, and not from the upload of a version.
      next.observability = v.metadata.observability || null;
      next.versions.set(v.id, v);
      next.deployment = [{ version_id: v.id, percentage: 100 }];
      scripts.set(name, next);
      return ok({ id: name });
    }
    if (!s) return bad(404, "no script " + name);
    if (rest === "" && request.method === "DELETE") return scripts.delete(name), ok(null);
    if (rest === "/versions") {
      const v = await version(s, request);
      if (v.metadata.migrations) return bad(400, "migrations only on the script upload");
      s.versions.set(v.id, v);
      return ok({ id: v.id });
    }
    if (rest === "/deployments" && request.method === "GET") return ok({ deployments: [{ versions: s.deployment }] });
    if (rest === "/deployments") return (s.deployment = (await request.json()).versions), ok({});
    if (rest === "/settings" && request.method === "GET") return ok({ bindings: live(s).metadata.bindings });
    if (rest === "/settings") {
      const patch = JSON.parse(await (await request.formData()).get("settings").text());
      const v = { id: "v" + ++n, metadata: { ...live(s).metadata, bindings: resolve(s, patch.bindings) }, parts: live(s).parts };
      s.versions.set(v.id, v);
      s.deployment = [{ version_id: v.id, percentage: 100 }];
      return ok({ bindings: v.metadata.bindings });
    }
    if (rest === "/script-settings") {
      if (request.method === "PATCH") s.observability = (await request.json()).observability;
      return ok({ observability: s.observability || null });
    }
    if (rest === "/subdomain") return (s.subdomain = (await request.json()).enabled), ok({});
    if (rest === "/schedules") return (s.schedules = await request.json()), ok({});
    return bad(404, "no route " + path);
  };
  const running = (name) => {
    const s = scripts.get(name);
    return s ? bindingOf(live(s), "BRAIN_INFO").json.hash : null;
  };
  return { fetch, scripts, log, calls, unhealthy, stored, d1, tokens, running, live: (name) => live(scripts.get(name)) };
}
// %%
// A deployer under simulate, with helpers to act as the holder of the recovery key and as the kernel.
deployerRig = async ({ acceptEmitted = true, config = {}, store } = {}) => {
  const fake = fakeCloudflare();
  const sim = await simulate(deployer_service, {
    secrets: { CF_API_TOKEN: "tok", RECOVERY_KEY: "rk" },
    config: { base: "cb", account: "acct", subdomain: "sub", owner: "did:plc:owner", self: "cb-deployer", pollMs: 0, tickGapMs: 0, pollTries: 2, acceptEmitted, ...config },
    rows: store,
    fetch: fake.fetch
  });
  const G = "https://cb-deployer.sub.workers.dev";
  const post = (url, body, headers) => sim.fetch(url, { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json", ...headers }, body: JSON.stringify(body) });
  const made = async (worker, role, salt, extra = {}) => {
    const parts = [{ path: "worker.js", text: "export default {} // " + salt }];
    const meta = { worker, role, crons: [], flags: [], methods: [], access: {}, paths: [], secrets: [], resources: [], bindings: [], ...extra };
    return { parts, meta, hash: await partsHash(parts, meta) };
  };
  return {
    fake,
    sim,
    made,
    recover: async (body) => (await post(G + "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.infra.apply", body, { authorization: "Bearer rk" })).json(),
    asOwner: async (method, body) => {
      const key = (sim.rows.get("worker/brain") || {}).key;
      const headers = { "x-brain-key": key, "x-brain-caller": "owner" };
      const r = body === undefined
        ? await sim.fetch("https://deployer.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.infra." + method, { headers })
        : await post("https://deployer.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.infra." + method, body, headers);
      return r.json();
    },
    form: (fields) => sim.fetch(G + "/", { method: "POST", body: new URLSearchParams(fields) }),
    state: async () => (await sim.fetch(G + "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.infra.getState", { headers: { authorization: "Bearer rk" } })).json()
  };
}
// %%
deployerAllowsExamples = [
  { given: { key: "worker/brain-x-whatsapp", op: "update" }, expect: null },
  { given: { key: "worker/brain-deployer", op: "delete" }, expect: 'resource name "brain-deployer" is reserved' },
  { given: { key: "worker/brain", op: "update" }, expect: 'resource name "brain" is reserved' },
  { given: { key: "worker/brain-core", op: "update" }, expect: 'resource name "brain-core" is reserved' },
  { given: { key: "queue/brain-x-jobs", op: "create" }, expect: 'unknown resource kind "queue"' },
  { given: { key: "worker/whatsapp", op: "create" }, expect: 'resource name "whatsapp" must match brain-x-[a-z0-9-]' },
  { given: { key: "r2_bucket/brain-x-blobs", op: "delete", objects: 412 }, expect: 'bucket "brain-x-blobs" holds 412 objects' },
  { given: { key: "r2_bucket/brain-x-scratch", op: "delete", objects: 0 }, expect: null },
  { given: { key: "worker/brain-deployer", op: "unchanged" }, expect: null }
]
// %%
test_deployerAllows_examples = {
  for (const e of deployerAllowsExamples) expect(deployerAllows(e.given)).toBe(e.expect);
  return deployerAllowsExamples.length + " examples";
}
// %%
test_probation_transitions = {
  const start = { state: "probation", version: "9c03d7e", lastGood: "4f2a91c", since: 0, fails: 0 };
  const run = (events) => events.reduce(nextKernelState, start);
  const min = 60 * 1000;
  expect(run([{ type: "tick", now: min, healthy: true }, { type: "confirm" }]).state).toBe("confirmed");
  expect(run([{ type: "tick", now: min, healthy: false }, { type: "tick", now: 2 * min, healthy: false }]).reason).toBe("health check failed twice");
  expect(run([{ type: "tick", now: min, healthy: false }, { type: "tick", now: 2 * min, healthy: true }]).state).toBe("probation");
  expect(run(Array.from({ length: 10 }, (_, i) => ({ type: "tick", now: (i + 1) * min, healthy: true }))).reason).toBe("not confirmed in 10 minutes");
  expect(nextKernelState({ state: "probation", version: "b", lastGood: "a", since: 0, fails: 0 }, { type: "tick", now: 90000, healthy: true, probationMs: 90000 }).reason).toBe("not confirmed in 90 seconds");
  expect(run([{ type: "tick", now: min, healthy: false }, { type: "tick", now: 2 * min, healthy: false }, { type: "confirm" }]).version).toBe("4f2a91c");
  return "5 cases";
}
// %%
test_only_the_deployer_names_the_cloudflare_token = {
  const e = await deployer_service.emit();
  expect(e.meta.worker).toBe("brain-deployer");
  expect(e.meta.secrets).toEqual(["CF_API_TOKEN", "RECOVERY_KEY"]);
  // The deployer carries the interpreter and what distilling needs; no other Worker does.
  expect(e.parts.map((p) => p.path)).toEqual(["worker.js", "lib/quickjs.js", "lib/distiller-data.js", "source.js", "quickjs.wasm"]);
  const rig = await deployerRig();
  // A recipe that names the token, or the deployer itself, is refused whoever asks.
  const sneaky = await rig.made("brain-x-sneaky", "recipe", "a", { secrets: ["CF_API_TOKEN"] });
  const self = await rig.made("brain-deployer", "deployer", "a");
  const out = await rig.recover({ workers: [sneaky, self] });
  expect(out.results.map((r) => r.state)).toEqual(["refused", "refused"]);
  expect(out.results[1].reason).toBe('resource name "brain-deployer" is reserved');
  expect(rig.fake.scripts.size).toBe(0);
  return out.results[0].reason;
}
// %%
test_apply_refusals = {
  const rig = await deployerRig();
  const cases = [
    [await rig.made("whatsapp", "recipe", "a"), 'resource name "whatsapp" must match brain-x-[a-z0-9-]'],
    [await rig.made("brain", "recipe", "a"), 'resource name "brain" is reserved'],
    [await rig.made("brain-core", "kernel", "a"), "role kernel must be named brain"],
    [await rig.made("brain-x-a", "recipe", "a", { resources: ["deployer"] }), 'a recipe may not use the platform cell "deployer"'],
    [{ ...(await rig.made("brain-x-a", "recipe", "a")), hash: "0".repeat(64) }, 'the parts sent for "brain-x-a" do not hash to 000000000000']
  ];
  const out = await rig.recover({ workers: cases.map((c) => c[0]) });
  expect(out.results.map((r) => r.reason)).toEqual(cases.map((c) => c[1]));
  expect(rig.fake.log.filter((l) => l.includes("/workers/")).length).toBe(0);
  return cases.length + " refusals, no Cloudflare call";
}
// %%
test_the_table_database_is_bound_to_brain_db_alone = {
  const rig = await deployerRig();
  expect((await rig.recover({ workers: [await rig.made("brain-core", "core", "c1")] })).results[0].state).toBe("deployed");
  // A Worker that uses sql reaches its tables through the core. It has no database binding.
  await rig.recover({ workers: [await rig.made("brain-x-m", "recipe", "m1", { resources: ["sql"] })] });
  expect(rig.fake.live("cb-x-m").metadata.bindings.map((b) => b.name).sort()).toEqual(["BRAIN_CONFIG", "BRAIN_INFO", "BRAIN_KEY", "CORE"]);
  // brain-db has the table database, named as its script is, beside the Brain's one database for rows.
  expect((await rig.recover({ workers: [await rig.made("brain-db", "system", "d1", { resources: ["database", "rows"] })] })).results[0].state).toBe("deployed");
  const db = Object.fromEntries(rig.fake.live("cb-db").metadata.bindings.map((b) => [b.name, b]));
  expect([db.SQL.id, db.DB.type, db.DB.id, rig.fake.d1.map((d) => d.name)]).toEqual(["d1-1", "d1", "d1-2", ["cb-sql", "cb-db"]]);
  // No other Worker may name it, whatever its role.
  const no = await rig.recover({ workers: [await rig.made("brain-x-n", "recipe", "n1", { resources: ["database"] }), await rig.made("brain-other", "system", "o1", { resources: ["database"] })] });
  expect(no.results.map((r) => [r.state, r.reason])).toEqual([["refused", "only brain-db is bound to the table database"], ["refused", "only brain-db is bound to the table database"]]);
  return db.DB.id;
}
// %%
test_a_browser_is_bound_shown_before_approval_and_not_for_a_member = {
  const rig = await deployerRig();
  await rig.recover({ workers: [await rig.made("brain", "kernel", "k1"), await rig.made("brain-core", "core", "c1")] });
  // Held for approval, the page says that the service opens browsers and that they cost money.
  const one = await rig.made("brain-x-web", "recipe", "w1", { resources: ["browser", "rows"] });
  expect((await rig.asOwner("apply", { workers: [one] })).results[0].state).toBe("waiting");
  const shown = await (await rig.sim.fetch("https://cb-deployer.sub.workers.dev/")).text();
  expect(shown).toContain("<b>Opens remote browsers.</b> Cloudflare bills browser time to this account.");
  expect((await rig.form({ key: "rk", action: "approve:" + one.hash })).status).toBe(200);
  expect((await rig.asOwner("apply", { workers: [one] })).results[0].state).toBe("deployed");
  const names = () => rig.fake.live("cb-x-web").metadata.bindings.map((b) => b.type + ":" + b.name).filter((b) => b.includes("X_")).sort();
  expect(names()).toEqual(["browser:X_CF_BROWSER_RUN"]);
  // A second deploy binds it once: it is not also carried over as a binding to a Worker.
  expect((await rig.recover({ workers: [await rig.made("brain-x-web", "recipe", "w2", { resources: ["browser", "rows"] })] })).results[0].state).toBe("deployed");
  expect(names()).toEqual(["browser:X_CF_BROWSER_RUN"]);
  // A service that does not reach the cell has no such binding, and its page entry has no such line.
  const plain = await rig.made("brain-x-plain", "recipe", "p1", { resources: ["rows"] });
  await rig.asOwner("apply", { workers: [plain] });
  expect((await (await rig.sim.fetch("https://cb-deployer.sub.workers.dev/")).text())).not.toContain("Opens remote browsers");
  return names()[0];
}
// %%
test_every_upload_turns_logs_on_and_the_invocation_line_off = {
  const rig = await deployerRig();
  await rig.recover({ workers: [await rig.made("brain", "kernel", "k1"), await rig.made("brain-core", "core", "c1"), await rig.made("brain-x-a", "recipe", "a1")] });
  const of = (name) => rig.fake.scripts.get(name).observability, ON = { enabled: true, logs: { enabled: true, invocation_logs: false } };
  for (const name of ["cb", "cb-core", "cb-x-a"]) expect(of(name)).toEqual(ON);
  // A script from before logs: Cloudflare does not take the setting from a version, so the deployer sets it on the script.
  rig.fake.scripts.get("cb-x-a").observability = null;
  rig.fake.scripts.get("cb-core").observability = { enabled: true, logs: { enabled: true, invocation_logs: true } };
  const patches = () => rig.fake.log.filter((l) => l.startsWith("PATCH") && l.endsWith("/script-settings")).length;
  await rig.recover({ workers: [await rig.made("brain-x-a", "recipe", "a2"), await rig.made("brain-core", "core", "c2")] });
  expect([of("cb-x-a"), of("cb-core"), patches()]).toEqual([ON, ON, 2]);
  // Already on: not set again.
  await rig.recover({ workers: [await rig.made("brain-x-a", "recipe", "a3")] });
  expect(patches()).toBe(2);
  return "3 new scripts, 2 scripts set, 1 left as it was";
}
// %%
test_a_declared_cloudflare_permission_is_held_for_the_owner_and_minted_for_that_worker_alone = {
  const rig = await deployerRig();
  await rig.recover({ workers: [await rig.made("brain", "kernel", "k1"), await rig.made("brain-core", "core", "c1"), await rig.made("brain-x-plain", "recipe", "p1")] });
  const READ = ["Workers Observability Read"], BOTH = ["Workers Observability Read", "Workers Tail Read"];
  const logs = (salt, cloudflare = READ) => rig.made("brain-x-logs", "recipe", salt, { cloudflare });
  // Held for the owner also when deploys need no approval, and the page names the permission.
  await rig.form({ key: "rk", action: "approval:off" });
  const one = await logs("l1");
  expect((await rig.asOwner("apply", { workers: [one] })).results[0].state).toBe("waiting");
  expect(rig.fake.tokens.size).toBe(0);
  expect(await (await rig.sim.fetch("https://cb-deployer.sub.workers.dev/")).text()).toContain("<b>Cloudflare permissions: Workers Observability Read.</b>");
  await rig.form({ key: "rk", action: "approve:" + one.hash });
  expect((await rig.asOwner("apply", { workers: [one] })).results[0].state).toBe("deployed");
  // One token: exactly the declared group, of the account kind, on this account, ending in 90 days.
  const [t1] = [...rig.fake.tokens.values()];
  expect(rig.fake.tokens.size).toBe(1);
  expect(t1.policies).toEqual([{ effect: "allow", resources: { "com.cloudflare.api.account.acct": "*" }, permission_groups: [{ id: "g-obs" }] }]);
  expect(Math.round((new Date(t1.expires_on) - Date.now()) / 86400000)).toBe(90);
  // The value is bound to that Worker and is nowhere else: not in another Worker, not in the deployer's rows.
  const bound = (name) => rig.fake.live(name).metadata.bindings.find((b) => b.name === "CF_TOKEN");
  const config = (name) => rig.fake.live(name).metadata.bindings.find((b) => b.name === "BRAIN_CONFIG").json;
  expect(bound("cb-x-logs")).toEqual({ type: "secret_text", name: "CF_TOKEN", text: t1.value });
  expect([bound("cb"), bound("cb-core"), bound("cb-x-plain")]).toEqual([undefined, undefined, undefined]);
  expect([config("cb-x-logs").account, config("cb-x-plain").account]).toEqual(["acct", undefined]);
  expect(JSON.stringify([...rig.sim.rows])).not.toContain(t1.value);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.get("token/brain-x-logs")).toMatchObject({ id: t1.id, groups: READ });
  const events = () => rig.sim.rows.get("audit/tokens").map((a) => a.event + " " + a.token);
  expect(events()).toEqual(["mint " + t1.id]);
  // The same set again: the token is kept.
  expect((await rig.recover({ workers: [await logs("l2")] })).results[0].state).toBe("deployed");
  expect([[...rig.fake.tokens.keys()], bound("cb-x-logs").text]).toEqual([[t1.id], t1.value]);
  // 30 days or less left: a new token, and the one before is deleted.
  rig.sim.rows.set("token/brain-x-logs", { ...rig.sim.rows.get("token/brain-x-logs"), expires: Date.now() + 29 * 86400000 });
  await rig.recover({ workers: [await logs("l3")] });
  const [t2] = [...rig.fake.tokens.values()];
  expect([rig.fake.tokens.size, t2.id !== t1.id, bound("cb-x-logs").text]).toEqual([1, true, t2.value]);
  // Another set: a new token of that set.
  await rig.recover({ workers: [await logs("l4", BOTH)] });
  const [t3] = [...rig.fake.tokens.values()];
  expect([rig.fake.tokens.size, t3.policies[0].permission_groups]).toEqual([1, [{ id: "g-obs" }, { id: "g-tail" }]]);
  expect(events()).toEqual(["mint " + t1.id, "roll " + t2.id, "delete " + t1.id, "mint " + t3.id, "delete " + t2.id]);
  // A deploy that is put back leaves the token as it was.
  const broken = await logs("l5", READ);
  rig.fake.unhealthy.add(broken.hash);
  expect((await rig.recover({ workers: [broken] })).results[0].state).toBe("put-back");
  expect([[...rig.fake.tokens.keys()], bound("cb-x-logs").text]).toEqual([[t3.id], t3.value]);
  // The service removed: no token.
  await rig.recover({ remove: ["brain-x-logs"] });
  expect([rig.fake.tokens.size, rig.sim.rows.has("token/brain-x-logs"), events().at(-1)]).toEqual([0, false, "delete " + t3.id]);
  return events().length + " audit rows";
}
